WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='4913e813-feb1-5691-8b99-945b4e5088c7' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT 'ac76fe29-5118-5527-9402-d12a37baa6cd','Mold staining','Discoloration and marking of a tape and its packaging left by fungal (mould) growth, where hyphae and their pigments and metabolic by-products stain the surface and can etch or weaken the binder, often persisting after the visible mould is removed. It indicates past or active biological deterioration driven by high humidity.','Mould is a fungus that can grow on tape kept in damp conditions. As it grows it leaves marks and stains on the surface. These stains can remain even after the mould is cleaned off. The growth can also weaken the tape''s coating.','The staining is a visible warning of mould activity and of damp storage, and it flags a tape that needs careful, protected cleaning before playback. It also signals possible lasting damage to the coating.','Finding a stained, musty reel, a technician isolates it, cleans it under proper containment with protective equipment, and corrects the storage humidity to stop further growth.','Biological deterioration',ARRAY['Relative humidity','Localized dry-air treatment','Tape cleaning','Binder hydrolysis','Magnetic coating']::text[],ARRAY['UNSAFE: Handling or cleaning mouldy tape without gloves, a fitted respirator, and containment such as a fume hood or open air, exposing the worker to harmful spores','Assuming that wiping the mould away undoes the damage, when staining and binder etching can remain','Returning a cleaned reel to the same damp store, letting mould regrow','Using household bleach or unknown biocides on tape, which can attack the coating']::text[],ARRAY['Assessing a musty reel from a damp basement store','Cleaning a mould-affected tape under containment before transfer','Correcting storage humidity after mould is found']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='ac76fe29-5118-5527-9402-d12a37baa6cd' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Mold staining'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT 'ac76fe29-5118-5527-9402-d12a37baa6cd','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='ac76fe29-5118-5527-9402-d12a37baa6cd' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '8c669f40-81b3-5f33-85bf-08d1111e1692','Oxide shedding','The loss of magnetic oxide (pigment) particles and binder from the surface of a magnetic tape during handling or playback, caused by deterioration of the binder that normally holds the pigment to the backing. As the binder loses cohesive strength, commonly through binder hydrolysis (sticky-shed syndrome), the magnetic coating rubs off, leaving deposits on guides and heads and causing dropouts and permanent signal loss.','A tape''s magnetic layer is glued to its plastic backing by a binder. When that binder breaks down, the coating rubs off as the tape plays. This debris clogs the heads and leaves gaps in the sound. Once it sheds, that signal is gone for good.','Recognizing oxide shedding tells an archivist that a tape''s binder has failed and that each pass strips away irreplaceable signal, so the tape must be stabilized before it is played.','A technician who sees brown or black powder on the guides and heads, or hears dropouts, stops, cleans the path, and evaluates the tape for binder treatment before any transfer.','Media deterioration',ARRAY['Sticky-shed syndrome','Binder hydrolysis','Tape baking','Dropout','Print-through','Particle agglomerate']::text[],ARRAY['Continuing to play a shedding tape, so each pass strips off more coating and permanently loses more signal.','UNSAFE: Baking a shedding tape without confirming its binder type; baking treats polyester-urethane binder hydrolysis only and can destroy acetate- or paper-based tapes or tapes degrading by other means.','UNSAFE: Handling or cleaning tape with visible mould without personal protective equipment (nitrile gloves and a respirator); mould on tape is a biohazard and is easily mistaken for oxide shedding.','Wiping the magnetic surface hard or with the wrong material, which abrades the fragile coating and removes more oxide.']::text[],ARRAY['Finding brown powder deposits on the heads and guides after playing an old reel.','Deciding whether a deteriorated master needs binder treatment before transfer.','Cleaning the tape path between passes on a shedding archival tape.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='8c669f40-81b3-5f33-85bf-08d1111e1692' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Oxide shedding'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT '8c669f40-81b3-5f33-85bf-08d1111e1692','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='8c669f40-81b3-5f33-85bf-08d1111e1692' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '014a4d3b-77c3-5256-830a-6e7745e4d778','Pack collapse','A structural failure of the wound tape pack in which loosely or unevenly wound layers lose their mutual support and slump, telescope, or cave inward, so the pack no longer holds a firm, even cylindrical form. It leaves layers displaced and edges unsupported, promoting cinching, creasing, and edge damage when the tape is handled or played.','Tape is wound onto a reel as a firm, even roll called the pack. If it is wound too loose, that roll can slump or cave in. The layers slide out of place and the edges lose support. Playing a collapsed pack can crease and crush the tape.','The idea flags that a poorly wound pack has lost its shape and can no longer protect the tape, prompting a careful, even rewind before storage or playback.','On finding a slumped or telescoped pack, a technician winds the tape slowly at even tension on a well-aligned machine to rebuild a firm pack rather than playing it as found.','Tape pack defects',ARRAY['Tape pack','Cinching','Pack slip','Telescoping','Winding tension','Retensioning']::text[],ARRAY['Fast-winding a collapsed, slack pack to tidy it, which lets the loose layers slip and crease.','Storing a reel with a collapsed pack flat, so the unsupported layers sag and the edges get crushed.','Assuming a loose pack is harmless, when uneven support leads to cinching, popped strands, and dropouts.']::text[],ARRAY['Receiving an archival reel wound so loosely that the pack has slumped.','Rebuilding a firm pack by retensioning before transfer.','Inspecting stored reels for loose, caved-in winding.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='014a4d3b-77c3-5256-830a-6e7745e4d778' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Pack collapse'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT '014a4d3b-77c3-5256-830a-6e7745e4d778','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='014a4d3b-77c3-5256-830a-6e7745e4d778' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '2d0d69aa-4191-5c23-a24a-c3a79ff87f55','Pack compression','The compressive stress imposed on the inner layers of a tape pack by the winding tension of the outer layers. In a tightly wound or over-tensioned pack, accumulated radial pressure can compress and deform the inner turns, producing spoking (radial kinks) and layer-to-layer print-through, and, in degraded tape, blocking, especially when the pack is stored under fluctuating temperature.','When tape winds tightly onto a reel, each layer squeezes the layers beneath it. Near the center this squeezing pressure adds up. Too much pressure can kink the inner turns and copy sound between layers. Winding at the right tension keeps that pressure safe.','Understanding pack compression explains why over-tight winding damages the inner layers and why archival tapes are wound at a controlled, moderate tension.','A technician sets a moderate, even winding tension and avoids storing tightly wound reels in warm conditions to limit the pressure that spokes or prints the inner layers.','Tape pack defects',ARRAY['Spoking','Winding tension','Pack stress','Print-through','Tape pack','Blocking']::text[],ARRAY['Winding archival tape very tight for a neat pack, which raises inner-layer pressure and causes spoking and print-through.','Storing tightly wound reels in a warm place, so heat and pressure together deform the pack.','Reading radial spoke lines through the flange as damage to the plastic reel rather than compression of the tape turns.']::text[],ARRAY['Seeing radial spoke lines when looking through the reel flange.','Choosing a moderate winding tension for long-term storage.','Diagnosing print-through that is worse in the tightly wound inner layers.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='2d0d69aa-4191-5c23-a24a-c3a79ff87f55' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Pack compression'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT '2d0d69aa-4191-5c23-a24a-c3a79ff87f55','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='2d0d69aa-4191-5c23-a24a-c3a79ff87f55' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '1b2372e8-0422-50b2-ac5c-2f3ae86da513','Pack dish','A lateral deformation of the tape pack in which the wound layers shift sideways relative to one another so the flat face of the pack takes on a dished or coned profile rather than a flat plane. It arises from uneven winding tension, an unevenly slit or cupped tape, or dimensional changes under temperature and humidity swings, and it can force tape edges against the reel flange, causing edge damage.','A tape pack should have a flat, even side face. Dishing is when the wound layers drift sideways into a shallow bowl or cone shape. It comes from uneven winding, or from heat and damp changing the tape. The bulging edges can rub the reel flange and get damaged.','Naming dishing helps a technician spot sideways pack deformation early and correct the winding before the tape edges are crushed or folded.','Seeing a dished pack, a technician rewinds the tape at even tension and stores it upright in stable temperature and humidity to keep the pack face flat.','Tape pack defects',ARRAY['Pack slip','Pack shift','Flange pack','Winding tension','Tape pack','Edge damage']::text[],ARRAY['Playing a badly dished pack, so the offset edges ride against the flange and crease or curl.','Storing reels where temperature and humidity swing, which drives the pack to dish.','Winding at uneven tension, which lets the layers creep sideways into a dish.']::text[],ARRAY['Inspecting a reel whose pack face is coned rather than flat.','Correcting a dished pack by an even library wind before transfer.','Choosing stable storage conditions to prevent dishing.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='1b2372e8-0422-50b2-ac5c-2f3ae86da513' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Pack dish'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT '1b2372e8-0422-50b2-ac5c-2f3ae86da513','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='1b2372e8-0422-50b2-ac5c-2f3ae86da513' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT 'bb76ce68-3f40-501d-b026-427a571a88bb','Pack recovery','The restoration of a deformed or unevenly stressed tape pack to a firm, even, stable wound form, typically achieved by unspooling and rewinding (retensioning) the tape at a controlled, uniform tension and speed. The process redistributes interlayer stresses and relieves conditions such as cinching, pack slip, or uneven tension before storage or transfer.','A tape pack can lose its even shape or build up uneven stress over time. Pack recovery means winding the tape back into a firm, even roll. You unspool it and rewind it slowly at a steady tension. This evens out the pressure and settles the pack before storage.','It returns an at-risk pack to a safe, even condition so the tape can be stored or played without the layers slipping, kinking, or creasing.','Before transferring a neglected reel, a technician does a slow, even retensioning wind on an aligned machine to recover a firm pack rather than playing it as found.','Tape pack defects',ARRAY['Retensioning','Winding tension','Pack slip','Cinching','Tape pack','Pack relaxation']::text[],ARRAY['Fast-winding to recover a pack, which jerks the layers and can cinch or crease the tape instead of settling it.','Skipping a recovery wind and playing a deformed pack directly, so slipped or kinked layers shed and drop out.','UNSAFE: Retensioning a shedding or sticky tape before it is stabilized, which strips coating onto the guides and can seize the transport.']::text[],ARRAY['Retensioning a long-stored reel to rebuild an even pack before transfer.','Relieving cinching and uneven tension with a controlled rewind.','Preparing a deformed archival pack for safe storage.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='bb76ce68-3f40-501d-b026-427a571a88bb' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Pack recovery'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT 'bb76ce68-3f40-501d-b026-427a571a88bb','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='bb76ce68-3f40-501d-b026-427a571a88bb' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT 'db616e25-157e-5a94-9662-1014014790e2','Pack relaxation','The gradual, time-dependent easing of interlayer stress in a wound tape pack as the viscoelastic tape backing creeps and stress-relaxes under sustained winding tension. Over long storage this redistribution can slacken or tighten regions of the pack unevenly, contributing to pack slip, cinching, or windowing, and it is one reason archival tapes are periodically retensioned.','Plastic tape slowly gives a little under steady pressure. In a wound reel, the stress between layers eases and shifts over months and years. Some parts loosen while others tighten. That uneven change can let layers slip, so archives rewind old tapes now and then.','The concept explains why a pack''s tension does not stay constant in storage and why periodic retensioning helps keep the pack stable.','Knowing packs relax over time, an archivist schedules periodic inspection and retensioning of stored masters and rewinds any that have slackened unevenly.','Tape pack defects',ARRAY['Retensioning','Winding tension','Pack slip','Cinching','Windowing','Pack stress']::text[],ARRAY['Assuming a pack keeps its original tension forever, so stored reels are never inspected or retensioned.','Winding very tight to compensate for future relaxation, which instead causes spoking and print-through.','Storing reels flat, so relaxing layers sag sideways and dish.']::text[],ARRAY['Inspecting decades-old masters for slack that developed in storage.','Scheduling periodic retensioning of an archival tape collection.','Explaining why a once-firm reel now shows pack slip.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='db616e25-157e-5a94-9662-1014014790e2' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Pack relaxation'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT 'db616e25-157e-5a94-9662-1014014790e2','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='db616e25-157e-5a94-9662-1014014790e2' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '53eb10d2-7bca-5768-9dbe-44f41ab79e22','Pack scatter','An irregular, disorganized winding of the tape pack in which individual layers or strands are laterally displaced and stand proud of the pack face rather than lying in a smooth, flush cylinder. Often the result of winding a nicked or unevenly slit tape, or winding at low or uneven tension, it produces popped strands and exposed edges that are vulnerable to creasing and edge damage.','A good pack has all its layers lined up flush and smooth. In a scattered wind, strands sit out of line and poke out from the side. It comes from loose or uneven winding, or a damaged tape edge. Those sticking-out strands are easy to bend and crush.','Spotting pack scatter warns that the tape was wound poorly and has exposed, vulnerable edges, prompting a clean, even rewind before storage.','Finding a scattered pack, a technician winds a smooth, flush pack at even tension and checks for popped strands and edge damage before storing the reel.','Tape pack defects',ARRAY['Popped strand','Pack slip','Winding tension','Tape pack','Edge damage','Cinching']::text[],ARRAY['Fast-winding a scattered pack, which snags the protruding strands and folds or tears them.','Storing a reel with proud, popped strands, so the exposed edges get crushed against the box or flange.','Blaming a scattered wind on the machine when a nicked or unevenly slit tape edge is the cause.']::text[],ARRAY['Receiving a reel whose pack face is ragged with protruding strands.','Rewinding a smooth, flush pack before archival storage.','Inspecting the pack edge for popped strands after a fast wind.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='53eb10d2-7bca-5768-9dbe-44f41ab79e22' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Pack scatter'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT '53eb10d2-7bca-5768-9dbe-44f41ab79e22','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='53eb10d2-7bca-5768-9dbe-44f41ab79e22' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '567e08f0-27cb-5076-81aa-47dbb91080d0','Pack shift','A lateral, side-to-side displacement of part or all of a tape pack, in which groups of windings move together across the width of the reel, leaving a stepped or offset pack face. Caused by uneven winding tension, shock, or dimensional change in storage, pack shift can bring tape edges into contact with the reel flange and cause edge damage on playback.','In a pack shift, a block of wound layers slides sideways together. This leaves a step or ledge on the flat face of the pack. It comes from uneven winding, a knock, or heat and damp. The shifted edges can hit the reel side and get damaged when played.','The term helps a technician read a stepped pack face as a handling or winding fault and correct it before the offset edges are damaged.','Seeing a stepped, offset pack, a technician rewinds the tape evenly and stores it upright and supported to stop the layers shifting again.','Tape pack defects',ARRAY['Pack slip','Pack dish','Flange pack','Winding tension','Tape pack','Edge damage']::text[],ARRAY['Playing a shifted pack, so the stepped edges ride the flange and crease.','Dropping or knocking reels, which jolts blocks of winding sideways.','Storing reels loose or flat, letting the pack creep sideways over time.']::text[],ARRAY['Finding a stepped ledge across the face of a stored pack.','Rewinding an offset pack before transfer.','Diagnosing edge damage traced to a shifted pack riding the flange.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='567e08f0-27cb-5076-81aa-47dbb91080d0' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Pack shift'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT '567e08f0-27cb-5076-81aa-47dbb91080d0','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='567e08f0-27cb-5076-81aa-47dbb91080d0' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '0debe8da-5876-5a13-8982-1e7344abb9a2','Pack slip','A lateral slip of selected windings within an otherwise smooth tape pack, producing high or low spots across the pack face when the reel is laid flat. Because the affected turns unwind unevenly and can make contact with the reel flange, pack slip leads to edge damage such as creasing, curling, or folding when the tape is played.','In a smooth pack, all the layers line up. Pack slip is when some layers slide sideways, making bumps or dips across the flat face. Those slipped layers can rub the reel side as they unwind. That rubbing bends and creases the tape edge.','Recognizing pack slip lets a technician expect uneven unwinding and edge contact, and correct the pack before the tape is damaged in playback.','Finding high and low spots on the pack face, a technician rewinds an even pack at controlled tension and watches for flange contact and edge damage during transfer.','Tape pack defects',ARRAY['Cinching','Pack shift','Popped strand','Winding tension','Tape pack','Flange pack']::text[],ARRAY['Playing a slipped pack as found, so the raised turns ride the flange and crease.','Fast-winding to smooth the pack, which can cinch the loose, slipped layers.','Storing reels at uneven or low tension, which invites layers to slip sideways.']::text[],ARRAY['Spotting high and low spots across a pack laid flat.','Rewinding an even pack before playback to avoid flange contact.','Diagnosing edge creasing caused by slipped windings.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='0debe8da-5876-5a13-8982-1e7344abb9a2' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Pack slip'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT '0debe8da-5876-5a13-8982-1e7344abb9a2','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='0debe8da-5876-5a13-8982-1e7344abb9a2' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '062a2f11-770b-50b3-ba92-7af02c48c263','Pack stress','The mechanical stress, force per unit area (for example pounds per square inch), carried between the layers of a wound tape pack as a result of winding tension. Tape wound at high tension produces high interwinding (radial) stress that presses the layers together; excessive or uneven pack stress promotes deformation, spoking, blocking, and print-through, while too little leaves a slack, unstable pack.','Winding tape onto a reel presses the layers together. That squeezing force between layers is the pack stress. Too much stress deforms and kinks the layers and copies sound between them. Too little leaves the pack loose and floppy. Archives aim for a steady middle amount.','The concept sets the target for how firmly tape should be wound: enough to hold a stable pack, but not so much that the layers deform or print through.','A technician chooses a moderate, even winding tension so the pack holds its shape without building the high stress that spokes or blocks the inner layers.','Tape pack defects',ARRAY['Winding tension','Pack compression','Spoking','Print-through','Blocking','Tape pack']::text[],ARRAY['Winding very tight for a firm pack, which raises interlayer stress and causes spoking and print-through.','Winding too loose to protect the tape, which leaves a slack pack that slips and cinches.','Storing high-stress packs in warm conditions, where heat plus stress causes blocking and deformation.']::text[],ARRAY['Setting winding tension on a transport before an archival wind.','Explaining why over-tight reels spoke and print through.','Balancing a firm versus a slack pack for long-term storage.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='062a2f11-770b-50b3-ba92-7af02c48c263' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Pack stress'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT '062a2f11-770b-50b3-ba92-7af02c48c263','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='062a2f11-770b-50b3-ba92-7af02c48c263' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '3bd23061-8f7f-583c-af47-ff39e2f15d95','Pack tension','The winding tension applied to the tape as it is spooled onto the reel, the force (or force per unit tape width) that determines how tightly the pack is wound. Correct, uniform pack tension holds the layers in a firm, even, stable pack; tension that is too high creates excessive interlayer stress with spoking and print-through, while tension too low or uneven produces a slack pack prone to slip, cinching, and scatter.','Pack tension is how hard the tape is pulled as it winds onto the reel. It sets how tight the finished roll is. The right, steady tension makes a firm, even pack. Too tight kinks and copies the layers; too loose lets them slip and fold.','It is the key control an archivist sets when winding tape, balancing a firm, stable pack against the risk of over-tight, high-stress winding.','A technician sets and checks a moderate, even winding tension on the transport so archival reels wind into firm, flat, stable packs.','Tape pack defects',ARRAY['Pack stress','Winding tension','Retensioning','Spoking','Pack slip','Tape pack']::text[],ARRAY['Setting winding tension too high, which over-stresses the pack and causes spoking and print-through.','Setting it too low or letting it vary, which leaves a slack, uneven pack that slips and cinches.','Ignoring transport tension calibration, so packs wind inconsistently across a collection.']::text[],ARRAY['Calibrating transport tension before winding archival masters.','Choosing an even library-wind tension for storage.','Troubleshooting slack or over-tight packs from a mis-set transport.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='3bd23061-8f7f-583c-af47-ff39e2f15d95' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Pack tension'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT '3bd23061-8f7f-583c-af47-ff39e2f15d95','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
