SELECT '178fb0a5-217b-5713-8608-6e1b609e8c93','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='178fb0a5-217b-5713-8608-6e1b609e8c93' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT 'f298b1f4-e2b7-5553-81e8-473c9f832a61','Pellon wiping','A manual tape-cleaning technique in which the tape is drawn slowly through the tape path or across a held pad of Pellon, a soft lint-free nonwoven fabric, so that loose debris, shed oxide, and surface residue are wiped away without abrading the magnetic coating. The Pellon can be mounted in the tape path of a spooling machine or applied by hand during a slow, even wind.','Pellon is a soft, lint-free cloth. The old tape is spooled slowly past a pad of it. The cloth gently wipes off loose dust and flakes. This helps the tape play cleanly without scratching it.','It removes loose surface contamination and shed particles that would otherwise clog the replay heads or scratch the tape, improving signal recovery while avoiding the coating loss caused by aggressive cleaning machines.','Before transferring an archival reel, a technician mounts a Pellon pad in the tape path or wipes the tape during a slow library-wind pass, checking the pad for oxide and grime and changing it as it loads up.','Cleaning',ARRAY['Pigment shedding','Sticky-shed syndrome','Library wind','Print-through','Reel replacement']::text[],ARRAY['Using a coarse or linting material instead of a true lint-free nonwoven fabric, which sheds fibres onto the tape or scratches the coating.','Wiping hard or fast, which can burnish or strip a fragile magnetic layer instead of gently lifting loose debris.','UNSAFE: Hand-wiping visibly mouldy tape without a respirator, gloves, and containment, since tape mould is a biohazard that requires proper personal protective equipment.','UNSAFE: Reaching for alcohol or other solvents as a first cleaning step, which can dissolve binders and lubricants and expose the worker to harmful fumes; cleaning should begin with dry methods.']::text[],ARRAY['Preparing a decades-old open-reel master for digitisation by removing loose oxide before it reaches the heads.','Cleaning a dusty field-recording tape recovered from long uncontrolled storage.','Reducing head-clogging dropouts during a difficult transfer of a shedding tape.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='f298b1f4-e2b7-5553-81e8-473c9f832a61' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Pellon wiping'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT 'f298b1f4-e2b7-5553-81e8-473c9f832a61','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='f298b1f4-e2b7-5553-81e8-473c9f832a61' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT 'a3fd91a1-7c49-5945-8ccb-c8c515b19e59','Pigment layer','The magnetic top coat of a tape, consisting of magnetic pigment, fine particles such as gamma ferric oxide, cobalt-modified iron oxide, chromium dioxide, or metal particles, dispersed in a polymer binder and applied over the base film. It is the layer in which the recorded signal is stored as patterns of magnetisation.','This is the coating that actually holds the sound. It is made of tiny magnetic specks stuck in a glue-like binder. The specks store the recording as magnetism. It sits on top of the clear plastic backing.','It carries the recorded information: the magnetic particles retain the field patterns written by the record head, and the binder holds them in place while letting the tape run smoothly over the heads.','A technician judges the pigment layer''s condition, checking for shedding, softening, or loss of output, to decide whether a tape needs cleaning, treatment, or a careful single-pass transfer.','Tape Structure',ARRAY['Binder hydrolysis','Pigment shedding','Sticky-shed syndrome','Polyester base','Backcoat','Magnetic coating']::text[],ARRAY['Confusing the pigment layer, which is the magnetic coating, with the base film, which is the clear plastic carrier beneath it.','Assuming all pigment layers are equally stable, when metal-particle and chromium-dioxide coatings degrade faster and lose output more readily than iron-oxide coatings.','Believing the visible brown or black colour indicates recording quality, when pigment type and binder condition matter far more.']::text[],ARRAY['Inspecting a reel for signs of binder failure before playback.','Explaining why a metal-particle cassette has lost high-frequency output over decades.','Diagnosing head clogs caused by a softening pigment layer.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='a3fd91a1-7c49-5945-8ccb-c8c515b19e59' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Pigment layer'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT 'a3fd91a1-7c49-5945-8ccb-c8c515b19e59','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='a3fd91a1-7c49-5945-8ccb-c8c515b19e59' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '2effaa2f-c647-5bc4-b6e5-72188b24ecf3','Pigment shedding','The loss of magnetic pigment from the tape coating, in which particles or flakes of the magnetic layer come loose and deposit on heads, guides, and the tape path. It arises when the binder loses cohesion, through age-related embrittlement of old cellulose-acetate binders (dry shedding) or hydrolysis of polyurethane binders (wet, sticky shedding).','Shedding means the magnetic coating starts to flake off the tape. Bits of it rub onto the machine parts. It happens when the glue holding the coating breaks down. The tape then plays with dropouts and clogged heads.','As a failure mode it signals binder breakdown; recognising it tells the archivist that the coating is no longer securely held and that playback risks depositing the recording onto the heads and losing signal.','A technician watches for brown or black powder building up on the heads and guides during a pass, stopping to clean and reassessing whether the tape needs treatment before further playback.','Physical Degradation',ARRAY['Sticky-shed syndrome','Binder hydrolysis','Pigment layer','Pellon wiping','Dropout']::text[],ARRAY['Continuing to play a shedding tape without cleaning, so shed material clogs the heads and buries the signal in dropouts.','Assuming all shedding is sticky-shed, when dry shedding from old acetate binders is a different mechanism that baking does not fix.','UNSAFE: Handling heavily degraded or mouldy shedding tape without gloves and respiratory protection.']::text[],ARRAY['A 1970s reel leaves a trail of oxide on the heads within seconds of play.','Deciding whether a shedding tape needs baking or simply careful cleaning.','Cleaning the tape path repeatedly during a one-pass archival transfer.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='2effaa2f-c647-5bc4-b6e5-72188b24ecf3' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Pigment shedding'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT '2effaa2f-c647-5bc4-b6e5-72188b24ecf3','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='2effaa2f-c647-5bc4-b6e5-72188b24ecf3' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '6ae3f8fd-1f59-52f2-a66e-7176905570a3','Pinch-roller eccentricity','A defect in a tape machine''s rubber pinch roller in which the roller is not perfectly round or not concentric with its shaft, so its effective radius varies as it rotates. Pressing the tape against the capstan, an eccentric roller imparts a cyclic speed variation, producing wow and flutter at the roller''s rotational frequency.','The pinch roller is a rubber wheel that presses the tape onto the drive shaft. If the wheel is worn lopsided, it grips unevenly as it spins. That makes the tape speed up and slow down in a steady wobble. You hear it as a wavering pitch.','Recognising roller eccentricity as a cause of periodic speed error lets the technician trace unwanted pitch wobble to the transport rather than the tape, and correct it by servicing or replacing the roller.','When a transfer shows regular pitch wavering, a technician checks the pinch roller for hardening, flat spots, or off-centre wear and replaces it, since aged or alcohol-hardened rollers are a known flutter source.','Transport Fault',ARRAY['Wow and flutter','Reel eccentricity','Capstan','Scrape flutter','Library wind']::text[],ARRAY['Blaming the tape for pitch wobble when a worn or eccentric pinch roller in the machine is the real cause.','Cleaning original rubber rollers with alcohol, which hardens and embrittles them over time and increases wow and flutter.','Ignoring a glazed or flat-spotted roller because playback still runs, allowing avoidable speed error into the transfer.']::text[],ARRAY['Diagnosing a cyclic pitch waver during an archival transfer.','Servicing a long-stored open-reel deck before a preservation project.','Comparing flutter rates to identify which rotating part is at fault.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='6ae3f8fd-1f59-52f2-a66e-7176905570a3' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Pinch-roller eccentricity'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT '6ae3f8fd-1f59-52f2-a66e-7176905570a3','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='6ae3f8fd-1f59-52f2-a66e-7176905570a3' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT 'b030aabd-50f6-5191-91da-9eab98f7c1ca','Plasticizer migration','The gradual loss of plasticizer from a plasticized tape polymer as the plasticizer diffuses to the surface and exudes or evaporates, removing the flexibility it provided so the material stiffens and embrittles. It is a documented deterioration mechanism of cellulose-acetate base film and a recognised long-term risk for plasticized polyvinyl-chloride base.','Some plastics have a softener added to keep them bendy. Over many years that softener slowly leaks out to the surface. As it leaves, the plastic backing turns stiff and brittle. The tape can then crack or warp.','As a degradation concept it explains why certain acetate and PVC tapes grow brittle or distorted with age; understanding it guides the cool, stable storage that slows plasticizer loss.','An archivist finding a stiff, brittle, or exuding tape treats plasticizer loss as a likely cause, handles the reel gently to avoid cracking, and prioritises it for careful transfer.','Chemical Degradation',ARRAY['Cellulose acetate base','Polyvinyl-chloride base','Vinegar syndrome','Binder hydrolysis','Lubricant loss']::text[],ARRAY['Confusing plasticizer loss with lubricant loss; both leave the tape surface, but they are different additives with different effects.','Assuming polyester (PET) tape suffers plasticizer migration, when PET is not plasticized and does not lose plasticizer the way acetate and PVC can.','UNSAFE: Forcing a brittle, plasticizer-depleted tape through a machine, which can snap it and damage both the recording and the transport.']::text[],ARRAY['Assessing a stiff 1950s acetate reel that has become brittle in storage.','Explaining surface exudation or bloom on an old tape.','Setting cool, stable storage to slow further plasticizer loss.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='b030aabd-50f6-5191-91da-9eab98f7c1ca' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Plasticizer migration'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT 'b030aabd-50f6-5191-91da-9eab98f7c1ca','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='b030aabd-50f6-5191-91da-9eab98f7c1ca' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT 'bc8c2506-7488-5a8f-a977-0d74c2c7d65a','Polyester base','A tape backing made of oriented polyester film, polyethylene terephthalate (PET), marketed as Mylar, introduced for audio and video tape from about 1960 and now the dominant base material. It is mechanically robust and chemically stable, highly resistant to oxidation and hydrolysis, but it stretches (shoelaces) under excessive stress before it breaks.','This is the clear plastic strip that carries the magnetic coating. It is made of a strong, stable plastic called polyester. It resists moisture and ageing far better than older backings. But if pulled too hard it stretches instead of snapping, which ruins the sound.','The base film gives the tape its strength and dimensional stability; polyester replaced acetate and PVC because it is tougher and far more resistant to chemical breakdown, greatly extending tape life.','Recognising a reel as polyester tells the technician the backing is likely stable, but warns that a jammed or over-tensioned pass can permanently stretch it, so transport tension must be set carefully.','Tape Structure',ARRAY['Polyvinyl-chloride base','Cellulose acetate base','Pigment layer','Tape stretch','Vinegar syndrome']::text[],ARRAY['Assuming polyester tape is indestructible; it resists chemical decay but can still be permanently stretched or deformed by poor winding and excess tension.','Confusing the polyester (PET) base with the polyester-polyurethane binder; the stable base and the hydrolysis-prone binder are different parts of the tape.','Treating a stretched polyester tape as recoverable, when stretched sections, unlike a clean acetate break, are usually unrecoverable.']::text[],ARRAY['Identifying base type when triaging a mixed collection for preservation risk.','Setting safe tension to avoid stretching a thin long-play polyester tape.','Explaining why a post-1960 master is chemically stable yet still mistracks after a bad wind.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='bc8c2506-7488-5a8f-a977-0d74c2c7d65a' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Polyester base'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
