WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='e64ff93f-a3c0-51b3-ba82-0e63a0843ba9' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '50efd0a6-ca7d-57a0-8881-4e9218d5a3d5','Sticky-shed syndrome','A degradation of the tape binder, driven by hydrolysis of its polyester-polyurethane polymer, in which the binder absorbs moisture, softens, and loses cohesion. Affected tape becomes tacky, sheds gummy residue onto guides and heads, shows high friction, squeal, and stick-slip, and can seize in the transport.','Sticky-shed is when the glue-like binder holding a tape together goes bad. The tape gets sticky and gummy. It squeals, sheds bits onto the machine, and can even jam as it plays.','Naming this failure lets an archivist diagnose why a tape is tacky and unplayable and choose a temporary treatment, such as controlled baking, to recover the recording.','A technician who finds a squealing, tacky reel identifies sticky-shed and, for the affected polyester types, incubates it at controlled low heat before a prompt transfer.','Tape Degradation',ARRAY['Binder hydrolysis','Stick-slip motion','Tape baking','Squeal','Print-through']::text[],ARRAY['UNSAFE: Baking acetate or lacquer media, which the sticky-shed baking process is not designed for and can damage.','UNSAFE: Handling mouldy or heavily degraded tape without gloves and a fitted respirator.','Playing a sticky tape untreated, which sheds oxide and clogs the heads.','Treating baking as permanent, when the effect is temporary and the tape must be copied within days.']::text[],ARRAY['A polyester master from the 1970s or 1980s squealing and shedding residue.','Gummy deposits building on guides and heads during playback.','Baking an affected reel to enable a one-time preservation transfer.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='50efd0a6-ca7d-57a0-8881-4e9218d5a3d5' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Sticky-shed syndrome'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT '50efd0a6-ca7d-57a0-8881-4e9218d5a3d5','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='50efd0a6-ca7d-57a0-8881-4e9218d5a3d5' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '8d704dae-d2d2-5d41-be8b-8f451417bec4','Storage set','A permanent deformation that tape acquires from being held wound under tension for long periods, so it retains the curvature and pack distortions of the reel it was stored on. Prolonged tape-pack stress, aggravated by temperature and humidity cycling, relaxes and reshapes the base film, which can cause curl, edge weave, and mistracking on playback.','Leave tape wound tightly for years and it keeps that shape. This is storage set. The tape holds a curl or bend from the reel, which can make it wander or mistrack when played.','It explains why a long-stored tape may not lie flat or track properly; understanding it supports periodic retensioning and stable storage to limit permanent deformation.','Facing a tape with set-in curl, a technician retensions and acclimatises it, then plays it gently, accepting that severe set may not fully relax.','Tape Deformation',ARRAY['Tape pack','Retensioning','Cinching','Curvature error','Substrate']::text[],ARRAY['Storing reels for decades without periodic retensioning to relieve stress.','Storing tape flat or in unstable heat and humidity, which deepens the set.','Expecting a badly set tape to return fully to flat after a single rewind.']::text[],ARRAY['A decades-old reel holding a curl from its storage pack.','Edge weave and mistracking from base-film set on playback.','Retensioning stored reels every few years to limit permanent set.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='8d704dae-d2d2-5d41-be8b-8f451417bec4' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Storage set'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT '8d704dae-d2d2-5d41-be8b-8f451417bec4','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='8d704dae-d2d2-5d41-be8b-8f451417bec4' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT 'fb4d2bd3-344c-51ce-8a33-e42b917ad3d7','Substrate shrinkage','A permanent reduction in the length and/or width of a magnetic tape''s base film (substrate) caused by aging, loss of plasticiser or moisture, or prolonged exposure to heat and low humidity. In cellulose-acetate tapes it accompanies vinegar-syndrome decomposition; in polyester (PET) tapes heat can cause non-recoverable shrinking of the oriented base film. The change alters recorded track geometry and degrades tape-to-head contact.','The plastic base that carries the recording can slowly get shorter or narrower as it ages. Heat, dryness, and chemical breakdown all cause this. When the base shrinks, the recorded tracks no longer line up with the head. That makes the sound weak or distorted.','Recognising substrate shrinkage explains why an aged tape mistracks or plays at the wrong length, and it drives decisions on cool, stable storage and on transferring at-risk tapes before the loss becomes permanent.','An engineer who finds an acetate reel playing short, or a videotape mistracking, checks for substrate shrinkage and adjusts storage, handling and transfer priority accordingly.','Substrate deformation',ARRAY['Vinegar syndrome','Tape relaxation','Backing deformation','Tensilized polyester','Cupping']::text[],ARRAY['Assuming polyester tape is immune to dimensional change; heat can cause non-recoverable shrinking and stretching of PET base film too.','Confusing reversible temperature or humidity dimensional changes with permanent, aging-related shrinkage.','UNSAFE: Warming or baking a shrunken acetate tape to make it play; heat accelerates acetate decomposition and can destroy the recording.']::text[],ARRAY['An acetate reel from the 1950s plays back shorter than its logged running time.','A helically scanned videotape mistracks after storage in a hot, dry attic.','An archive tightens temperature and humidity limits to slow shrinkage across its tape holdings.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='fb4d2bd3-344c-51ce-8a33-e42b917ad3d7' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Substrate shrinkage'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT 'fb4d2bd3-344c-51ce-8a33-e42b917ad3d7','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='fb4d2bd3-344c-51ce-8a33-e42b917ad3d7' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT 'f5faaab4-ba82-536b-afbd-76cab186caa9','Tape baking','A conservation treatment in which a hydrolysis-degraded (''sticky-shed'') magnetic tape is held in a thermostatically stable, controlled low-temperature oven, typically around 50 C (122 F) at very low humidity for several hours up to a few days, to temporarily re-firm the binder so the tape can be played and transferred. The improvement is temporary and the procedure suits polyester-based reel and computer tapes suffering binder hydrolysis, not other tape types or defects.','Some old tapes get sticky and squeal because their glue-like binder has soaked up water. Baking gently warms the tape in a temperature-controlled oven for hours. This dries and firms the binder just long enough to play the tape. The fix does not last, so the tape is copied right away.','It exists to make a sticky, unplayable tape survive a safe pass through a machine so its content can be digitised before the binder fails again.','Before transferring a squealing 1980s master, an engineer bakes it in a laboratory oven at about 50 C, then copies it to a preservation file within days.','Conservation treatment',ARRAY['Sticky-shed syndrome','Binder hydrolysis','Tape squeal','Print-through','Tissue wiping']::text[],ARRAY['UNSAFE: Baking tape in a domestic kitchen oven or a microwave; their poor, cycling temperature control can overheat and permanently deform or erase the tape.','UNSAFE: Baking acetate or unaffected tapes; baking targets polyester binder hydrolysis only and can cause further damage on the wrong tape type, so expert advice is required first.','Treating baking as a permanent cure instead of transferring the content within days, after which the tape turns sticky again.','Baking repeatedly for routine playback; each session slightly damages the tape, so it is reserved for preservation transfers.']::text[],ARRAY['A studio master from the 1980s squeals and sheds oxide, so it is baked before a one-time digitisation.','An archive builds a controlled laboratory-oven protocol for batches of sticky reel-to-reel tapes.','A computer data tape suffering binder hydrolysis is baked to recover its files.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='f5faaab4-ba82-536b-afbd-76cab186caa9' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Tape baking'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT 'f5faaab4-ba82-536b-afbd-76cab186caa9','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='f5faaab4-ba82-536b-afbd-76cab186caa9' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT 'adc2f843-8071-54fa-a1ec-426f2f9dc937','Tape polishing','A mechanical surface treatment in which a tape is run under tension across a blade or burnishing surface to remove loose oxide, shed and surface asperities and to smooth the magnetic coating. Because it abrades and removes part of the top oxide layer, it was developed for reconditioning tapes for re-use and is generally not recommended for archival originals.','Tape polishing runs the tape across a fine blade or smoothing surface. This scrapes off loose bits and flattens rough spots on the surface. It can make a worn tape play more smoothly. But it also shaves off some of the recording layer, so archives usually avoid it on originals.','It aims to restore smooth tape-to-head contact and reduce dropouts on a worn or contaminated tape by physically cleaning and levelling its surface.','A technician may meet tape-polishing (burnishing) machines from the tape-reuse era and must decide against running an irreplaceable archival tape through one.','Conservation treatment',ARRAY['Tissue wiping','Tape squeal','Sticky-shed syndrome','Dropout','Oxide shedding']::text[],ARRAY['UNSAFE: Running an irreplaceable archival original across an abrasive polishing or burnishing blade; it permanently removes oxide and recorded signal.','Assuming polishing cures sticky-shed; hydrolysis is a chemical binder fault that abrasion cannot fix and may worsen.','Confusing gentle lint-free cleaning with abrasive polishing that cuts into the coating.']::text[],ARRAY['An archive inspects a donated deck fitted with a tape-polishing blade and disables it for preservation work.','A worn broadcast cartridge with heavy shedding is assessed for cleaning versus abrasive polishing.','A technician documents that a unique tape must never be polished before its only transfer.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='adc2f843-8071-54fa-a1ec-426f2f9dc937' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Tape polishing'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT 'adc2f843-8071-54fa-a1ec-426f2f9dc937','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='adc2f843-8071-54fa-a1ec-426f2f9dc937' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT 'befd4b7a-cce8-5159-907f-cade2ea89c32','Tape relaxation','The gradual dimensional relaxation, or creep, of a magnetic tape''s base film and wound pack when winding tension is too low or is not properly maintained, allowing the backing to slacken, stretch and deform. Such relaxation and deformation of the backing cause mistracking on videotape and speed- or level-related distortion on audio tape.','Tape needs to be wound with steady, even tension. If the wind is too loose, the plastic backing slowly slackens and changes shape. This is called relaxation. A relaxed, deformed tape no longer sits properly against the head, so playback mistracks or sounds wrong.','Understanding tape relaxation explains why loosely wound or poorly stored tapes deform, guiding the use of proper winding tension and stable storage to keep the pack dimensionally sound.','When a slackly wound reel plays with wow or mistracking, an engineer rewinds it at a controlled, even tension to redistribute pack stress before transfer.','Substrate deformation',ARRAY['Substrate shrinkage','Cinching','Pack slip','Backing deformation','Retensioning']::text[],ARRAY['Winding archival tape too loosely on the belief that low tension is always gentler; too little tension lets layers slip and the backing relax and deform.','Storing tapes flat so the pack sags, encouraging relaxation and pack slip.','Confusing recoverable relaxation from poor winding with permanent, aging-related shrinkage of the base film.']::text[],ARRAY['A reel stored loosely for years plays with wow until it is re-wound at proper tension.','An archive retensions large reels periodically to relieve pack stress.','A videotape mistracks after its pack slackened in storage.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='befd4b7a-cce8-5159-907f-cade2ea89c32' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Tape relaxation'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT 'befd4b7a-cce8-5159-907f-cade2ea89c32','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='befd4b7a-cce8-5159-907f-cade2ea89c32' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '7cd1e966-3a94-5d69-b784-317f3964f2f0','Tape skew','A deviation of the tape from its intended straight path across the heads, or a differential lengthwise displacement between simultaneously recorded tracks, caused by tape-guiding errors, uneven tension, edge damage or base-film deformation. Skew misaligns the tape relative to the head gap and, on multitrack recordings, introduces timing and phase errors between channels.','Skew means the tape does not travel straight and square across the head. It may wander sideways or twist. When this happens, the separate tracks stop lining up in time. Stereo or multitrack sound then loses its correct timing and image.','The concept lets technicians trace tracking and inter-channel timing faults to tape guiding, tension or deformation rather than to the original recording.','When a stereo master loses its centre image or a multitrack drifts out of phase, an engineer checks for skew by adjusting guides and tension and inspecting the tape edges.','Tracking defect',ARRAY['Mistracking','Azimuth error','Tape relaxation','Substrate shrinkage','Tension modulation']::text[],ARRAY['Blaming head azimuth for a timing problem actually caused by skew from worn guides or a deformed tape edge.','Forcing a skewing tape with extra tension, which can stretch or damage the edges further.','Overlooking edge damage as a cause of dynamic skew.']::text[],ARRAY['A quarter-inch stereo master shows shifting phase between channels during transfer.','A multitrack tape with a damaged edge skews and mistracks on replay.','An engineer aligns the tape guides to remove skew before digitising.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='7cd1e966-3a94-5d69-b784-317f3964f2f0' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Tape skew'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT '7cd1e966-3a94-5d69-b784-317f3964f2f0','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='7cd1e966-3a94-5d69-b784-317f3964f2f0' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '7b197ed8-1b67-5825-bb5f-2da44c4b38c9','Tape squeal','A high-pitched squealing or chirping produced when a tape sticks and slips rapidly against fixed guides and heads during transport, arising from excessive friction, most often from binder hydrolysis (''sticky-shed'') or from loss of the tape''s lubricant. The stick-slip motion also causes speed instability and can shed binder debris onto the tape path.','A squeal is a high, chirping sound a tape makes as it drags across the heads and guides. It happens when the tape is too sticky or has lost its built-in lubricant. The tape grabs and slips over and over, which makes the noise. If you hear it, stop playing to avoid more damage.','Squeal is an audible warning that a tape has become sticky or dry and is at risk, prompting the operator to stop and treat it before transfer.','Hearing a reel squeal on shuttle, an engineer stops at once and assesses it for baking or cleaning before attempting a transfer.','Binder degradation',ARRAY['Sticky-shed syndrome','Binder hydrolysis','Tape baking','Lubricant loss','Stick-slip']::text[],ARRAY['UNSAFE: Continuing to play a squealing, degraded tape; stick-slip and shedding damage the tape and clog heads, and if failure follows the playback head the content is lost.','Assuming squeal always means sticky-shed; loss of lubricant can also cause it and needs different handling.','Turning the level up to mask squeal instead of stopping and treating the tape.']::text[],ARRAY['A back-coated 1980s master squeals on the first shuttle and is set aside for baking.','A dry, older reel squeals from lubricant loss during transfer.','An operator halts playback the moment a chirping sound begins.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='7b197ed8-1b67-5825-bb5f-2da44c4b38c9' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Tape squeal'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT '7b197ed8-1b67-5825-bb5f-2da44c4b38c9','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='7b197ed8-1b67-5825-bb5f-2da44c4b38c9' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '2a496363-a231-5a73-99c7-fec901c58b43','Telescope','Telescoping is a winding defect in which the layers of a tape pack slip sideways relative to one another so that the pack protrudes from one side in a cone or ''telescope'' shape instead of presenting a flat, even edge. It results from a loose or uneven wind and from lateral shock or careless handling, especially of an unflanged pack, and it exposes the tape edges to bending and crushing.','A well-wound tape has flat, even sides. Telescoping is when the wound layers slide sideways and push out into a cone. It comes from a loose or uneven wind, or from knocking the reel. The pushed-out edges are then easily bent or crushed.','Spotting telescoping warns that a pack has lost its even wind and that the tape edges are vulnerable, prompting a careful, even re-wind before use.','Finding a telescoped tape pancake in a box, an archivist supports it flat and rewinds it slowly at even tension before any transfer.','Winding defect',ARRAY['Pack slip','Cinching','Popped strands','Tape relaxation','Flange pack']::text[],ARRAY['Fast-winding a telescoped tape to flatten it, which crushes and folds the protruding edges.','Storing unflanged tape pancakes flat, which lets the pack slump and telescope.','Confusing telescoping (sideways layer slip) with cinching (folded or wrinkled tape from a sudden stop).']::text[],ARRAY['A boxed tape pancake arrives telescoped after shipping and must be re-wound carefully.','A loosely wound reel telescopes after being stored on its side.','An archivist withholds a telescoped tape from immediate playback until it is re-tensioned.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='2a496363-a231-5a73-99c7-fec901c58b43' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Telescope'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT '2a496363-a231-5a73-99c7-fec901c58b43','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='2a496363-a231-5a73-99c7-fec901c58b43' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '93218c5a-2a0d-5f3c-af9f-b9faca35dda2','Tensilized polyester','Polyester (polyethylene terephthalate, PET) base film that has been pre-stretched, or ''tensilized'', to orient its molecules and raise its tensile strength in the lengthwise (machine) direction. Tensilizing permits a thinner, stronger base for long-play reel and cassette tapes, but the pre-stretched film is more prone to lengthwise deformation and curl under heat or tension than balanced (non-tensilized) polyester.','Tensilized polyester is tape backing that was stretched during making to make it stronger the long way. This lets makers use a thinner, longer tape that still resists snapping. The trade-off is less stability under stress. The stretched plastic deforms and curls more easily when hot or pulled hard.','It was developed so more playing time could fit on a reel or cassette without the thin tape breaking, by strengthening the base film along its length.','Handling thin long-play reels or C-120 cassettes, a technician treats tensilized-polyester tape gently because it stretches and curls more readily than standard tape.','Base film material',ARRAY['Substrate shrinkage','Tape relaxation','Cupping','Backing deformation','PET base film']::text[],ARRAY['Applying high winding or playback tension to thin tensilized tape, which can stretch or curl it permanently.','Assuming all polyester tape behaves alike; tensilized film is thinner and less dimensionally stable than balanced PET.','Storing thin long-play tapes in hot conditions, which encourages curl and deformation.']::text[],ARRAY['A C-120 cassette on thin tensilized polyester stretches when a deck applies too much tension.','An archivist flags thin long-play reels as higher risk for deformation.','A transfer of a long-play tape uses a gentle-tension deck to avoid stretching.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='93218c5a-2a0d-5f3c-af9f-b9faca35dda2' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Tensilized polyester'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
INSERT INTO glossary_topics (glossary_id,achievement_id,is_primary)
SELECT '93218c5a-2a0d-5f3c-af9f-b9faca35dda2','be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e',true
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary_topics gt WHERE gt.glossary_id='93218c5a-2a0d-5f3c-af9f-b9faca35dda2' AND gt.achievement_id='be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e');
INSERT INTO glossary (id,term,definition,plain_english,purpose_function,practical_application,category,related_terms,common_mistakes,scenario_contexts,achievement_id)
SELECT '0df68d14-ca7e-56cd-a773-97493cdd433d','Tension modulation','Cyclic or irregular variation in a tape''s tension as it moves through the transport, caused by factors such as reel eccentricity, an uneven pack, sticking or worn guides, and capstan or roller irregularities. Because tension governs the intimacy of tape-to-head contact and the effective tape speed, its modulation produces fluctuations in reproduced level and in speed (wow and flutter).','As tape moves through a machine, the pull on it should stay steady. Tension modulation is when that pull keeps changing. An uneven reel, sticky tape, or worn parts can cause it. Because the pull affects head contact and speed, the sound then wavers in volume and pitch.','The idea helps technicians link wavering level and wow or flutter to unsteady tape tension in the transport rather than to the recording itself.','When playback level pumps or the pitch wavers, an engineer checks for tension modulation from a dirty guide, sticky tape or an eccentric reel.','Playback artefact',ARRAY['Tape squeal','Stick-slip','Tape skew','Wow and flutter','Retensioning']::text[],ARRAY['Blaming the recording for level or pitch wavering that is really caused by unsteady transport tension.','Ignoring dirty or worn guides and rollers that modulate the tension.','Over-tightening tension to stop the wavering, which risks stretching the tape.']::text[],ARRAY['A transferred reel shows pumping level from an eccentric take-up reel.','A slightly sticky tape causes wow as tension varies at the heads.','An engineer services the guides and rollers to steady tension before digitising.']::text[],'be9c2311-f9c7-4657-b34e-a2eee81eaf9e'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM glossary g WHERE g.id='0df68d14-ca7e-56cd-a773-97493cdd433d' OR regexp_replace(lower(g.term),'[^a-z0-9]','','g')=regexp_replace(lower('Tension modulation'),'[^a-z0-9]','','g'));
